cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Laurel corpus: English verse in TEI, with scansion and canonical references"
message: "If you use this corpus, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Dome
    given-names: Garrett
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE-ME/laurel-corpus"
url: "https://laurelpoetry.com"
abstract: >-
  416 works of public domain English verse encoded in TEI P5: 18,107 poems and
  1,201,730 lines, each line carrying both the stress the words settle and the
  stress its metre asks for. Every poem has a canonical reference naming its
  edition, on the CTS model, and a permanent identifier that survives re-titling.
  Around 1,700 poems carry line-level timings against public domain recordings.
keywords:
  - poetry
  - prosody
  - scansion
  - metre
  - TEI
  - digital humanities
  - public domain
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
